=3D"man"></a><h1>MAN ARPALERT</h1><h2>NAME</h2>arpalert - ARP traffic monit=
oring<h2>DESCRIPTION</h2>Arpalert uses ARP protocol monitoring to prevent u=
nauthorized connections on the local network.
If an illegal connection is detected, a program or script is launched, whic=
h could be used to send an alert message, for example.<h2>COMMAND LINE</h2>=
<dl><dt><b>-f config_file</b></dt><dd>Use this config file<br><br></dd><dt>=
<b>-i interface</b></dt><dd>Comma separated network interfaces to lesson<br=
><br></dd><dt><b>-p pid_file</b></dt><dd>Use this pid file. this file conta=
in a pid number of the arpalert session. if the file exist and his locked, =
the deamon do not run.<br><br></dd><dt><b>-e exec_script</b></dt><dd>Script=
 launched when an alert is send<br><br></dd><dt><b>-D log_level</b></dt><dd=
>The level logged. the level are bitween 0 (emergency) and 7 (debug). if 3 =
is selected all levels bitween 0 and 3 arre logged.<br><br></dd><dt><b>-l l=
eases_file</b></dt><dd>This file contain a dump of the mac address in memor=
y (see config file).<br><br></dd><dt><b>-m module file</b></dt><dd>Specify =
a module file to load<br><br></dd><dt><b>-d</b></dt><dd>Run as daemon<br><b=
r></dd><dt><b>-F</b></dt><dd>Run in foreground<br><br></dd><dt><b>-v</b></d=
t><dd>Watch on screen all the option selected (the options specified in con=
fig file and the default options)<br><br></dd><dt><b>-h</b></dt><dd>The hel=
p command line.<br><br></dd><dt><b>-w</b></dt><dd>Debug option: print a dum=
p of paquets captured.<br><br></dd><dt><b>-P</b></dt><dd>Set the interface =
in promiscuous mode (don't set this if only the arp analyse is used)<br><br=
></dd><dt><b>-V</b></dt><dd>Print version and quit</dd></dl><h2>CONFIGURATI=
ON FILE</h2>The config file contain 3 types of data: integer, string and bo=
olean. The boolean type can take values 'oui', 'true', 'yes', '1'
for the true values or 'non', 'no', 'false', '0' for the falses values.<dl>=
<dt><b>user</b> =3D arpalert</dt><dd>Use privileges separation whith this u=
ser<br><br></dd><dt><b>umask</b> =3D 177</dt><dd>Uses this mask for the fil=
es created<br><br></dd><dt><b>chroot dir</b> =3D /home/thierry/arp_test/</d=
t><dd>Use this directory for program jail<br>If this option is commented th=
e program does not chroot<br>The program read the config file and open the =
syslog socket before the chroot:<br>The kill -HUP does not run with chroot.=
<br>If the syslog program is restarted, the socket change and the arpalert =
syslog system can't be connect to the new socket:
the logs with syslog are disabled. Prefere to use the log file.<br>All the =
path file are relative to the chroot dir (but not the config file)<br><br><=
/dd><dt><b>log file</b> =3D /var/log/arpalert.log</dt><dd>The program log i=
nto this file<br>If this option is commented, the internal system log is no=
t used<br>The internal system logs can be used in same time that syslog.<br=
><br></dd><dt><b>log level</b> =3D 6</dt><dd>The level logged. the level ar=
e bitween 0 (emergency) and 7 (debug). if 3 is selected all levels between =
0 and 3 are logged.<br><br></dd><dt><b>use syslog</b> =3D true</dt><dd>If t=
his option is false, the syslog system is disabled<br><br></dd><dt><b>macli=
st file</b> =3D /etc/arpalert/maclist.allow</dt><dd>white list<br><br></dd>=
<dt><b>maclist alert file</b> =3D /etc/arpalert/maclist.deny</dt><dd>black =
list<br><br></dd><dt><b>maclist leases file</b> =3D /var/lib/arpalert/arpal=
ert.leases</dt><dd>dump fil<br><br></dd><dt><b>dump inter</b> =3D 5</dt><dd=
>minimun time to wait between two leases dump<br><br></dd><dt><b>auth reque=
st file</b> =3D /etc/arpalert/authrq.conf</dt><dd>list of authorized reques=
t"<br><br></dd><dt><b>lock file</b> =3D /var/run/arpalert.lock</dt><dd>pid =
file<br><br></dd><dt><b>dump paquet</b> =3D false</dt><dd>Only for debuggin=
g: this dump paquet received on standard output<br><br></dd><dt><b>daemon</=
b> =3D false</dt><dd>if is set to true, run the program as daemon<br><br></=
dd><dt><b>interface</b> =3D ""</dt><dd>Comma separated network interfaces t=
o lesson. If this value is not specified, the soft select the first interfa=
ce.<br><br></dd><dt><b>catch only arp</b> =3D TRUE</dt><dd>Configure the ne=
twork for catch only arp request.
The detection type "new_mac" is desactived.
This mode is used for CPU saving if Arpalert is running on a router<br><br>=
</dd><dt><b>mod on detect</b> =3D ""</dt><dd>Module file loaded by arpalert=
. This module is launched on each valid alert.
This system permit to avoid a costly fork/exec<br><br></dd><dt><b>mod confi=
g</b> =3D ""</dt><dd>this chain is transfered to the init function of modul=
e loaded<br><br></dd><dt><b>action on detect</b> =3D ""</dt><dd>Script laun=
ched on each detection. Parameters are: <b>mac adress of requestor</b>, <b>=
ip of requestor</b>, <b>supp. parm.</b>, <b>type of alert</b>
.IP
type of alert:<br><b>0:</b> IP change<br><b>1:</b> Mac address already dete=
cted but not in white list<br><b>2:</b> Mac address in black list<br><b>3:<=
/b> New mac address<br><b>4:</b> Unauthorized arp request<br><b>5:</b> Abus=
ive number of arp request detected<br><b>6:</b> Ethernet mac address differ=
ent from arp mac address<br><b>7:</b> Flood detected<br><b>8:</b> New mac a=
ddress whithout ip address<br><br></dd><dt><b>execution timeout</b> =3D 10<=
/dt><dd>script execution timeout (seconds)<br><br></dd><dt><b>max alert</b>=
 =3D 20</dt><dd>maximun simultaneous lanched script<br><br></dd><dt><b>dump=
 black list</b> =3D false</dt><dd>dump the black listed mac address in leas=
es file<br><br></dd><dt><b>dump white list</b> =3D false</dt><dd>dump the w=
hite listed mac address in leases file<br><br></dd><dt><b>dump new address<=
/b> =3D true</dt><dd>dump the new mac address in leases file<br><br></dd><d=
t><b>mac timeout</b> =3D 259200</dt><dd>after this time a mac adress is rem=
oved from memory (seconds) (default 1 month)<br><br></dd><dt><b>max entry</=
b> =3D 1000000</dt><dd>after this limit the memory hash is cleaned (protect=
 to arp flood)<br><br></dd><dt><b>anti flood interval</b> =3D 10</dt><dd>th=
is permit to send only one mismatch alert in this time (in seconds)<br><br>=
</dd><dt><b>anti flood global</b> =3D 50</dt><dd>if the number of arp reque=
st in seconds exceed this value, all alerts are ignored for
"anti flood interval" time<br><br></dd><dt><b>mac vendor file</b> =3D ""</d=
t><dd>This file contain the association from mac address to vendor name. Th=
is file can be
downloaded here: http://standards.ieee.org/regauth/oui/oui.txt<br><br></dd>=
<dt><b>log mac vendor</b> =3D false</dt><dd>log vendor name<br><br></dd><dt=
><b>alert mac vendor</b> =3D false</dt><dd>give vendor name to script<br><b=
r></dd><dt><b>mod mac vendor</b> =3D false</dt><dd>give vendor name to modu=
le<br><br></dd><dt><b>log referenced address</b>, <b>alert on referenced ad=
dress</b>, <b>mod on referenced address</b> =3D false</dt><dd>log/launch sc=
ript/call module if the adress is referenced in hash but is not in white li=
st<br><br></dd><dt><b>log deny address</b>, <b>alert on deny address</b>, <=
b>mod on deny address</b> =3D true</dt><dd>log/launch script/call module if=
 the mac adress is in black list<br><br></dd><dt><b>log new address</b>, <b=
>alert on new address</b>, <b>mod on new address</b> =3D true</dt><dd>log/l=
aunch script/call module if the adress isn't referenced<br><br></dd><dt><b>=
log mac change</b>, <b>alert on mac change</b>, <b>mod on mac change</b> =
=3D true</dt><dd>log/launch script/call module if the ip adress id differen=
t from the last arp request with the same mac adress<br><br></dd><dt><b>log=
 ip change</b>, <b>alert on ip change</b>, <b>mod on ip change</b> =3D true=
</dt><dd>log/launch script/call module if the ip adress id different from t=
he last arp request with the same mac adress<br><br></dd><dt><b>log unauth =
request</b>, <b>alert on unauth request</b>, <b>mod on unauth request</b> =
=3D true</dt><dd>unauthorized arp request: launch if the request are not au=
thorized in auth file<br><br></dd><dt><b>ignore unknown sender</b> =3D true=
</dt><dd>dont analyse arp request for unknow hosts (not in white list)<br><=
br></dd><dt><b>ignore self test</b> =3D true</dt><dd>Ignore ARP self test g=
enerated by windows dhcp for unauthorized request detection<br><br></dd><dt=
><b>ignore me</b> =3D true</dt><dd>ignore arp request with mac adresse of t=
he listened interfaces for the authorizations checks<br><br></dd><dt><b>una=
uth ignore time method</b> =3D 2</dt><dd>select suspend time method:<br>1: =
ignore all unauth alerts during "anti flood interval" time<br>2: ignore onl=
y tuple (mac address, ip address) during "anti flood interval" time<br><br>=
</dd><dt><b>log request abus</b>, <b>alert on request abus</b>, <b>mod on r=
equest abus</b> =3D true</dt><dd>log/launch script/call module if the numbe=
r of request per seconds are &gt; "max request"<br><br></dd><dt><b>max requ=
est</b> =3D 1000000</dt><dd>maximun request authorized by second<br><br></d=
d><dt><b>log mac error</b>, <b>alert on mac error</b>, <b>mod on mac error<=
/b> =3D true</dt><dd>log/launch script/call module if the ethernet mac addr=
ess are different than the arp amc address (only for requestor)<br><br></dd=
><dt><b>log flood</b> =3D true</dt><dd><b>alert on flood</b> =3D true
<b>mod on flood</b> =3D true
log/launch script/call module if have too many arp request per seconds</dd>=
</dl><h2>DATA FILES FORMATS</h2><dl><dt><b>/etc/arpalert/maclist.allow</b> =
and <b>/etc/arpalert/maclist.deny</b>:</dt><dd>all the line with # as a <b>=
first</b> caracter are ignored<br>The data on this file take this form<br>&=
lt;MAC_ADRESS&gt; &lt;IP_ADDRESS&gt; &lt;DEVICE&gt; [&lt;FLAG&gt; &lt;FLAG&=
gt; &lt;FLAG&gt; ...]<br>The available flags are:<br><b>ip_change:</b> Igno=
re ip change alert for this mac address<br><b>black_listed:</b> Ignore blac=
k list alerts for this mac address<br><b>unauth_rq:</b> Ignore unauthorized=
 requests for this mac address<br><b>rq_abus:</b> Ignore request abus for t=
his mac address<br><b>mac_error:</b> Ignore mac error for this mac address<=
br><b>mac_change:</b> Ignore mac change for this mac address<br><br></dd><d=
t><b>/etc/arpalert/authrq.conf</b>:</dt><dd>all the word after # caracter a=
re ignored<br>all the blank characters are ignored<br>The authorisations li=
st for one mac address begin by the mac address into brackets<br>All the ne=
xt values are ip hosts address or ip networks address (with /xx notion)<br>=
[&lt;MAC_ADRESS&gt; &lt;DEVICE&gt;] &lt;IP_ADRESS&gt;<br>&lt;IP_ADRESS&gt;/=
&lt;BITS&gt;<br></dd></dl><h2>FILES</h2><b>sbin/arpalert</b>: binary file<b=
r><b>etc/arpalert/arpalert.conf</b>: default config file<br><b>var/run/arpa=
lert.pid</b>: pid file<br><b>var/state/arpalert.leases</b>: leases file<br>=
<br><br><a name=3D"enhowto"></a><h1>English howto <small>(corrected by Chri=
s)</small></h1><p>You are the administrator of a big LAN for which physical=
 access is difficult to
control. You know that viruses and data theft can happen due to external ma=
chines
that connect to the LAN without authorization.
You must to monitor these illegal connections. This is where Arpalert can h=
elp you.</p><p>Start by downloading the Arpalert archive on the official we=
b site. You must compile
the source code because packages are not provided. A simple <code>./configu=
re --prefix=3D/usr/local/arpalert &amp;&amp; make &amp;&amp;
make install</code> with root privileges will install the application on yo=
ur computer. You
can specify the install base directory with the parameter --prefix after th=
e
./configure command. By default the base directory is /usr/local/arpalert.<=
/p><p>A default config file is located in /usr/local/arpalert/etc/arpalert/=
arpalert.conf.
These defaults parameters are usable in most configurations.</p><p>Continui=
ng with root privileges, launch the program with the command
/usr/local/arpalert/sbin/arpalert -d. The option -d launches the program in=
 daemon
mode. If you always want to run Arpalert in daemon mode, you must to edit c=
onfig
file and replace <code>daemon =3D false</code> by <code>daemon =3D true</co=
de>.
If you watch the /var/log/messages
file, you will see all the machines detected on the network. These machines=
 are
recorded in the /usr/local/arpalert/var/lib/arpalert/arpalert.leases file.<=
/p><p>When all the local network machines are discovered, copy the file
/usr/local/arpalert/var/lib/arpalert/arpalert.leases into the maclist.allow=
 file
(cat /usr/local/arpalert/var/lib/arpalert/arpalert.leases &gt;
/usr/local/arpalert/etc/arpalert/maclist.allow). Don't hesitate to add new =
mac
addresses to this file. Restart the deamon, and the program will run. Now a=
ll the
new computers detected are probably intruders and they are logged. You can =
run
Arpalert with a script to alert you by e-mail (for example). Script example=
s are in
the directory "scripts".</p><a name=3D"frhowto"></a><h1>French howto</h1><p=
>Vous =C3=AAtes administrateur d'un lan relativement vaste mais aux acc=C3=
=A8s particuli=C3=A8rements incontrolables.
Sachant que les contaminations virales et les vols de donn=C3=A9es viennent=
 le plus souvent de machines
etrang=C3=A8res au r=C3=A9seau qui se connectent sans autorisation, il faut=
 imp=C3=A9rativement monitorer ces
connexions illicites. C'est =C3=A0 ce niveau l=C3=A0 qu'intervient ArpAlert=
.</p><p>Commencez par t=C3=A9l=C3=A9charger la derni=C3=A8re r=C3=A9vision =
du programme sur le site officiel.
Vous devrez passer par les sources, les diff=C3=A9rentes formes de packagin=
g ne sont pas g=C3=A9r=C3=A9es.
Un traditionel <code>./configure --prefix=3D/usr/local/arpalert &amp;&amp; =
make &amp;&amp; make install</code>
avec les droits root installera l'application
sur votre machine. Vous pouvez pr=C3=A9ciser dans le ./configure l'emplacem=
ent du r=C3=A9pertoire de base,
par d=C3=A9faut celui ci sera /usr/local/arpalert.</p><p>Un fichier de conf=
iguration par d=C3=A9faut sera plac=C3=A9 dans /usr/local/arpalert/etc/arpa=
lert/arpalert.conf.
Celui ci est fonctionnel pour la plupart des configurations.</p><p>Toujours=
 sous le compte root, d=C3=A9mmarrez maintenant le programme par un simple =
/usr/local/arpalert/sbin/arpalert -d.
le -d permettra le lancement en mode daemon. Pour automatiser le mode deamo=
n au d=C3=A9marage editez le fichier de
configuration et remplacez la ligne daemon =3D false par daemon =3D true. V=
ous pouvez faire un tail -f /var/log/messages
(ou /var/log/syslog selon les distributions) et vous verrez toute les machi=
nes de votre r=C3=A9seau d=C3=A9tect=C3=A9es.
Ces nouvelles machines seront stock=C3=A9es dans le fichier /usr/local/arpa=
lert/var/lib/arpalert/arpalert.leases
quelques cat sur ce fichier vous laisserons voir la liste des machines dete=
ct=C3=A9es.</p><p>Lorsque toutes les machines du r=C3=A9seau local ont =C3=
=A9t=C3=A9 d=C3=A9couvertes recopiez le contenu de ce fichier dans le
fichier maclist.allow (cat /usr/local/arpalert/var/lib/arpalert/arpalert.le=
ases &gt; /usr/local/arpalert/etc/arpalert/maclist.allow),
n'h=C3=A9sitez pas =C3=A0 compl=C3=A9ter ce fichier =C3=A0 la main. Red=C3=
=A9marrez le d=C3=A9mon, l'application fonctionne. =C3=80 partir de mainten=
ant toutes
les nouvelles machines d=C3=A9tect=C3=A9es sont des intrus potentiel et un =
message sera =C3=A9mis dans les logs.</p><a name=3D"links"></a><h1>Links an=
